@flexiarg operator/own-the-oversight
@title Admit The Monitoring Miss Aloud When The Suspicion Confirms
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-aeh0Ba turn-x6vPMj; first proposed for: An earlier conditional suspicion (turn-YasvGu's 'if a default is set to astra') turns out true, and the operator had the chance to catch it earlier.
@why [agency/loud-failure]

! conclusion: When the suspicion confirms, attach the admission: what was missed and that it was yours to catch.

  + IF:
    The miss is his own, not the system's.

  + HOWEVER:
    The confirmation could be reported as pure vindication; saying 'I had missed' instead keeps the detection record honest — the safeguard (operator attention) failed this once, which matters for judging how much to trust it next time.

  + THEN:
    When the suspicion confirms, attach the admission: what was missed and that it was yours to catch.

  + BECAUSE:
    The operator-side instance of loud failure: the miss surfaces at the layer that caused it (his own monitoring) rather than being laundered into a correct-but-late diagnosis with no provenance.
